A standard tiddler without compound text. The `compound-field` procedure edits its ordinary fields; the type is given in the call because there is no `type:` header to read.

<table>
<tr><th>Email</th><td><<compound-field fieldName="email" mode="edit" type="email">></td></tr>
<tr><th>Birthday</th><td><<compound-field fieldName="birthday" mode="edit" type="date">></td></tr>
<tr><th>Category</th><td><<compound-field fieldName="category" mode="edit" type="option-personal-business">></td></tr>
</table>

In view mode the email is plain text without a type, <<compound-field fieldName="email">>, and a link with one: <<compound-field fieldName="email" mode="view" type="email">>
